<!-- 10. DELETING YOUR ACCOUNT                -->
<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="alt-bg" id="delete-account">
  <div class="section-sm">
    <div class="section-eyebrow">Section 10 — Deleting your account</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">If you decide to leave</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">Deleting your account is permanent and cannot be undone. Here's exactly what happens and how to do it, whether you're a buyer or a seller.</p>

    <div class="guide-two-col">
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:15.5px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px">How to delete your account</h3>
        <div class="mini-steps">
          <div class="mini-step">
            <div class="mini-step-num"></div>
            <div class="mini-step-body">
              <h4>Go to your profile</h4>
              <p>Sign in and open your profile page from the account menu.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mini-step">
            <div class="mini-step-num"></div>
            <div class="mini-step-body">
              <h4>Scroll to the Danger Zone</h4>
              <p>Near the bottom of your profile page, you'll find account-level actions, including <strong>Delete account</strong>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mini-step">
            <div class="mini-step-num"></div>
            <div class="mini-step-body">
              <h4>Confirm by typing DELETE</h4>
              <p>You'll be asked to type <strong>DELETE</strong> into a confirmation box — this is a deliberate extra step so deletion is never accidental.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mini-step">
            <div class="mini-step-num"></div>
            <div class="mini-step-body">
              <h4>Account and data are removed</h4>
              <p>Your account, listings, photos, and enquiry history are permanently deleted, and you're signed out and returned to the homepage.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px">
        <div class="callout-box danger">
          <h4><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 001.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 001.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 00-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>This cannot be undone</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>All of your listings, photos, and messages are permanently removed.</li>
            <li>Any active listings go offline immediately — buyers can no longer find or message you.</li>
            <li>Reviews you've left or received elsewhere are not automatically deleted, since they may relate to another party's record.</li>
            <li>Payment records are kept for a period as required by financial record-keeping rules, even after account deletion.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="callout-box">
          <h4><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="6" y="4" width="4" height="16"/><rect x="14" y="4" width="4" height="16"/></svg>Not ready to fully delete?</h4>
          <p>If you just want a break, sellers can <strong>pause all listings</strong> or sign out instead — both are reversible, unlike deletion. See <a href="#account">Managing your account</a> above.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="callout-box" style="margin-top:28px;max-width:760px">
      <h4><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M21 15a2 2 0 01-2 2H7l-4 4V5a2 2 0 012-2h14a2 2 0 012 2z"/></svg>Buyers without an account</h4>
      <p>If you only ever sent an enquiry as a guest (without creating a seller account), there's no account to delete — your conversation history is tied to your device via a private link, and you can simply stop using it. To have any personal data associated with your enquiries removed, contact us and we'll handle it directly.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

